<title>FINLAND: AAMULEHTI SAYS PROFITABILITY MERGER AIM.</title>
<headline>AAMULEHTI SAYS PROFITABILITY MERGER AIM.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish media group Aamulehti Oy CEO Matti Packalen said on Tuesday the group's merger with commercial television channel MTV Oy aimed at improved profitability, but declined to give any estimate or say how.</p>
<p>&quot;This is of course a sensitive issue,&quot; Packalen told a news conference. &quot;Naturally the merger targets improved profitability, but we have no cost savings estimate.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the merger as such would not lead to any lay-offs.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
